{
  "name": "Real estate: property managers and brokers in a metro, ready as a campaign draft",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Real estate: property managers and brokers in a metro, ready as a campaign draft\n\n### How it works\nOpen a new metro in one minute. The form asks for a city or postal code and a radius in miles. Argorant counts property managers, leasing and brokerage leaders and owners at real estate companies based within that radius. If the count is within max_people, the search is saved as a list named after the metro, a campaign draft with two short emails that mention the city is created, and once the list has filled it is added to the draft; above it, nothing is saved or spent and the form says so. Review the draft, attach mailboxes and launch in Argorant.\n\nCosts: free until the list is added, then 1 credit per new person.\n\n### Setup\n1. Install the community node **n8n-nodes-argorant** (tested with 0.3.0 on n8n 2.46.6): Settings > Community nodes > Install. Guide: https://github.com/argorant/n8n-nodes-argorant\n2. Add an **Argorant API** credential with a key from Argorant (Settings, API keys).\n3. Set max_people in **Settings** and edit the emails in **Create the campaign draft**.\n4. Activate and open the production URL of **Metro form**.\n\n### Customization\nChange the titles for other buyers, such as facilities or maintenance managers.",
        "height": 653,
        "width": 520,
        "color": 1
      },
      "id": "b2077d0d-41d5-4910-b288-12a881aba042",
      "name": "Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -620,
        -260
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Size the metro\nFree count within the radius, checked against max_people.",
